1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,641
Copy-trading bots tell you what to buy.

2
00:00:03,641 --> 00:00:05,321
None tell you why.

3
00:00:05,321 --> 00:00:09,242
WhaleIndex is the opposite of a black box.

4
00:00:09,642 --> 00:00:20,055
An index token on Arc, priced in USDC, mirroring top Hyperliquid whales.

5
00:00:20,055 --> 00:00:24,539
Four agents decide every cycle:

6
00:00:24,539 --> 00:00:29,890
Scorer, Allocator, Risk, Coordinator.

7
00:00:30,290 --> 00:00:35,990
This cycle the agents chose NOT to trade.

8
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:40,438
Risk vetoed all three proposals;

9
00:00:40,438 --> 00:00:43,358
the Coordinator held.

10
00:00:43,358 --> 00:00:51,838
The decision to do nothing is published, with full reasoning.

11
00:00:52,238 --> 00:00:57,201
Every cycle is hashed and anchored on-chain.

12
00:00:57,201 --> 00:01:02,840
Open the full record and read what each agent saw.

13
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:05,321
Don't trust the agent.

14
00:01:05,321 --> 00:01:06,449
Verify it.

15
00:01:06,849 --> 00:01:13,794
Connect a wallet and buy or redeem shares at the on-chain NAV,

16
00:01:13,794 --> 00:01:16,259
settled on Arc in ~1s.

17
00:01:16,259 --> 00:01:21,524
USDC is the gas token, so no separate fee coin.

18
00:01:21,924 --> 00:01:26,216
Arc settlement, USDC everywhere,

19
00:01:26,216 --> 00:01:33,325
CCTP routing and USYC yield (both mocked on testnet),

20
00:01:33,325 --> 00:01:36,141
plus a slashing bond.

21
00:01:36,141 --> 00:01:42,311
A proof-of-reasoning ledger with a buy button.
